4105 \langfenp4105 I saw Thracian horses fed human blood,}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 their stables crammed with mangled bodies,}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 and, once I\uc1 \u8217 ?d seen that, overpowered them,}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 and killed those horses and their master, too?}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 The huge Nemean lion now lies dead,}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 killed by these arms of mine, and with this neck\uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 I have held up heaven. Jupiter\uc1 \u8217 ?s cruel wife}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 may have grown tired of issuing orders\uc1 \u8212 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 I am still not tired of carrying them out. }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 But now I am facing some new disease}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 which courage, weapons, and power in war\uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 cannot resist. An all-consuming fire}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 roams deep inside my lungs and feeds itself}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 on every limb, and yet Eurystheus}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 is thriving. Are there men who still believe}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 the gods exist?\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\cs17 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \s38 \li0 \ri0 \sa80 \widctlpar \nooverflow \faroman \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs20 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 {\cs17 \fs20 \rtlch \ltrch \super1 \chftn }{\*\bkmkstart n15}{\*\bkmkend n15}{\fs20 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af5 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe1033 \langfenp1033 Hercules in this speech reviews some of his most famous exploits, most of them from his celebrated twelve labours. Busiris was a king of Egypt who sacrificed foreigners. Hercules, passing through Egypt, was arrested by Busiris but broke free and killed him. Antaeus was a Libyan giant who drew his strength from the earth. He challenged people to wrestle and then killed them. Hercules held Antaeus off the earth, from which he drew his strength, until Antaeus weakened and then Hercules killed him. Geryon was a herdsman with three bodies. Hercules, in his tenth labour, killed him with an arrow and took away his herds. Cerberus was a three-headed dog guarding the entrance to Hades. Hercules in his twelfth labour went down to Hades and dragged him up to earth. In the seventh labour, Hercules brought back to Eurystheus the Cretan bull, which was ravaging Crete. At Elis Hercules completed his fifth labour, cleansing the Augean stables. His sixth labour was to drive birds away from the Stymphalian lake. Parthenium was a mountain in Arcadia where Hercules carried out his third labour, capturing the deer with golden antlers. For his ninth labour Hercules brought back the belt of Hippolyta, queen of the Amazons. In his eleventh labour, Hercules brought back apples from the Hesperides. Capturing the Erymanthian Boar was Hercules\uc1 \u8217 ? fourth labour, and killing the Lyrnaean Hydra was his second labour. The Thracian horses were the mares of Diomedes, which Hercules captured and brought to Eurystheus in his eighth labour (Ovid\uc1 \u8217 ?s text says he killed them). Hercules\uc1 \u8217 ? first labour was to bring back the skin of an allegedly invincible lion rampaging around Nemea. Hercules visited Atlas, who supported the heavens on his shoulders, and temporarily relieved him of the burden. Eurystheus, king of Mycenae, was Hercules\uc1 \u8217 ? great enemy, who, on Juno\uc1 \u8217 ?s instructions, assigned Hercules the different labours. }}}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105  }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \par }\pard \plain \s41 \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \nooverflow \aspalpha \aspnum \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \tql \tx426 \tql \tx1276 \tql \tx1843 \tql \tx6521 \tql \tx8505 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 {\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \uc1 \u160 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \par }\pard \plain \s41 \li0 \ri0 \widctlpar \nooverflow \aspalpha \aspnum \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \tql \tx426 \tql \tx1276 \tql \tx1843 \tql \tx6521 \tql \tx8505 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 {\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ? When Hercules had spoken, }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \langfenp4105 he wandered across the heights of Oeta,}{\fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af0 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe4105 \lang